00-first: reading="I see all the books I've read this year in one place with a short note on what I thought of each one, This year, before December.\nWhy: I usually forget what I read by december.\nMust: The books I've read this year are included.\nMust: Each book has a short note on what I thought of it.\nMust not: It must not be fancy." focused={"id":"model-519996abe1f78ed8","text":"What would you check to know this is done?"}
00-first: reading="New users do not feel spammed by onboarding emails, during the first week.\nWhy: The unsubscribe rate keeps going up, while marketing values the emails.\nMust: onboarding emails are not eliminated entirely.\nMust not: new users feel spammed." focused={"id":"model-43498cf4c758f837","text":"What observable sign would show that new users no longer feel spammed?"}
00-first: reading="Learners leave a wrong answer feeling smarter rather than dumber, after a wrong answer.\nWhy: Learners currently see a red X and move on, feel dumb, and leave.\nMust: work on phones.\nMust not: include gamification." focused={"id":"model-0fc714bf70c564d3","text":"What observable sign would show that learners leave a wrong answer feeling smarter rather than dumber?"}
00-first: reading="I know in about 5 seconds whether yesterday went well, using useful changes per hour and possibly cost, in the morning when I open Tinkery.\nWhy: The ledger report is a wall of numbers, so I do not know what to do with it; the 6am job sometimes fails silently and I find out days later.\nMust: Useful changes per hour is included.\nMust: The result is not a dashboard.\nMust not: The result must not be a wall of numbers." focused={"id":"model-3818d3afb8d4c53b","text":"What should you be able to observe or decide that shows this is working?"}
00-first: reading="I start capturing thought dumps at night, including by voice when talking is faster than typing.\nWhy: Opening a terminal feels like work, and typing is harder when I am tired." focused={"id":"model-c9289e9e4a3562ff","text":"What would you observe to know this is working?"}
00-first: reading="I receive a delicious change ready for human review that considers the health of the code base and makes the next change easier.\nWhy: I want work across the entire continuum of agentic software development to have rigor, durability, cohesion, and verification, from brain dump, prompt, hunch, or intuition through a review-ready pull request.\nMust: The work serves as a meta harness.\nMust: The work is human first.\nMust: The work considers the forest, not just the trees." focused={"id":"model-8998d6d36794c546","text":"What observable check would tell you this is working?"}
00-first: reading="" focused={"id":"model-14272a9eb54ad36a","text":"Who should benefit from fixing onboarding?"}
01-answer: reading="Why: People sign up then never come back; like 70% never do a second session." focused={"id":"model-3a7ee45ac6319c1f","text":"What should become true for people who sign up: should more of them return for a second session, or is there another outcome you want?"}
02-answer: reading="People who sign up return for a second session within a week.\nWhy: People sign up then never come back; like 70% never do a second session.\nDone when: More than half come back within a week." focused=null
00-first: reading="My mom identifies whether a text is fake before tapping anything.\nWhy: She keeps receiving scam texts and almost clicked one yesterday.\nMust: She will not install apps.\nMust: It has to be dead simple, like one step.\nMust not: She must not feel lectured." focused={"id":"model-91504caae7102179","text":"What should you observe to know this is working—for example, your mom checks a suspicious text before tapping it?"}
00-first: reading="I get the same clippy results locally and on GitHub CI, during CI checks.\nWhy: The clippy version differs between CI and my laptop, so things pass locally and fail on GitHub; this happened twice this week.\nMust: The clippy version on CI matches the clippy version on my laptop." focused={"id":"model-fc65577a057af1f8","text":"What observable check should show that the clippy mismatch problem is resolved?"}
